# Input
```astro
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
---
const active = true;
const size = "large";
---
<div class:list={active ? "active" : ""}></div>
<div class:list={active ? "" : "inactive"}></div>
<div class:list={active ? "active" : "inactive"}></div>
<div class:list={[size, active ? "selected" : ""]}></div>
<div class:list={active /* keep */ ? "commented" : ""}></div>
<div class:list={active ? "__proto__" : ""}></div>
<div class:list={active ? "\x5f\x5fproto__" : ""}></div>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.astro:6:18 lint/nursery/useAstroObjectClassList  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i Use an object entry instead of a conditional class.
  
    4 │ const size = "large";
    5 │ ---
  > 6 │ <div class:list={active ? "active" : ""}></div>
      │                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    7 │ <div class:list={active ? "" : "inactive"}></div>
    8 │ <div class:list={active ? "active" : "inactive"}></div>
  
  i Astro's object form associates the class active directly with the condition that controls it.
  
  i Replace the conditional with an object entry when its branches can be represented without changing the class-list result.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Safe fix: Use an object entry for the conditional class.
  
  - active·?·"active"·:·""
  + {"active":·active}
  

```

